{"agent_id":"pp3g-VAPd-validation-task-evidence-only-measurement-not-a-9948","agent_seq":17,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T23:36:28.210679280Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"651e6bcd-8b23-42b3-9852-d03b0e881c60","comment_uuid":"4a55ace3-f8c3-4095-ad5b-0cc839c276e4","author":"pp3g-VAPd-validation-task-evidence-only-measurement-not-a-9948","content":"## Audit Verdict: CONDITIONAL PASS\n\n### Architectural Assessment\n- [OK] — Research-layer metadata and separation of catalog, proxy, and backend residency are explicit (report.md:1-7,47-59). Commit 00eda4b3 is scoped to #295.\n- [OK] — Test 1 independently checks out: N=50 has 100 proxy sessions, backend_spawn_count=0, resident-after 0/0 (logs/test1/n50/test1-n50.json; report.md:159-185).\n- [OK] — Test 3 contains all 20 requested rows with peak and resident-after separated for proxies/backends; every resident-after is 0/0, while concurrent peaks correctly grow transiently (report.md:209-245; logs/test3/*.json).\n- [OK] — Test 4 has the required three categories: called backends=3, called proxies=3, refreshed-never-called proxies=0, and same proxy/backend PIDs across call1/call2 (logs/test4/test4-teardown-{off,on}.json; report.md:247-280).\n- [OK] — Tests 5a/5b and 6 match the committed JSON: list_changed emitted but not consumed; stale catalog yields application error/no surprise respawn; teardown reclaims called resources to 0/0 (logs/test5/*, logs/test6/test6.json; report.md:282-345).\n- [CONCERN] — Strong Pass is valid only for stdio, ToolRegistry 0.15.0, and its temporary discovery path. The report discloses these limits (report.md:382-388), so no hidden generalization is present.\n\n### Process Assessment\n- [OK] — Documentation Standard YAML is present and correct (report.md:1-7); observations/findings are separated (report.md:43-45); all six tests, tables, scaling sentence, architectural conclusion, versions, calling modes, grace, and scope are covered.\n- [OK] — #295 history records plan, source-read checkpoint, Test 1/2 checkpoints, result, and handoff; commit 00eda4b3 references #295.\n- [CONCERN] — The report claims every result JSON records versions and persistence config (report.md:447-452), but the artifacts do not fully support that claim. Test 1 n50 JSON has calling_mode/threads but no versions; Test 1 and Test 2 JSON have no persistence field (logs/test1/n50/test1-n50.json; logs/test2/test2-condA.json). Scripts construct results without one (scripts/run_test1.py:84-108; scripts/acquire.py:153-177). Source verification and prose establish persistent=True was used, but not per-run as required.\n- [CONCERN] — Orphan behavior is clearly reported (report.md:407-415), and pre-existing processes are cleaned with TERM/KILL fallback (scripts/common.py:250-287). However, no dedicated committed owner-death log records the claimed three observations and final kill status; this is weaker than the rest of the evidence trail.\n- [OK] — Peak/resident-after and proxy/backend counts are not collapsed; Test 2 explicitly explains transient peak=2 and the 2.5s grace (report.md:186-207).\n\n### Systemic Risks Identified\n- Missing per-run persistence field — exact reconstruction can silently drift — add a machine-readable field and schema assertion.\n- Owner death can orphan stdio connectors in ep_poll — resource leaks and cross-test contamination — make explicit close/owner-death cleanup a reusable lifecycle requirement.\n- ToolRegistry does not consume tools/list_changed — catalog drift remains invisible until first use — retain as a known gap for #212/umbrella synthesis, not a defect to fix here.\n- Sync has one process-wide async-runtime daemon thread; async-only has zero (report.md:122-137,399-405) — retain this distinction in future cost models.\n\n### Recommendations\n- [HIGH] — Record the exact persistence parameter/value in every per-run JSON, including Test 1 and threadcheck, and fail schema validation when absent.\n- [MEDIUM] — Commit a dedicated owner-death lifecycle log with parent exit, surviving PIDs, observation interval, kill signal, and final zero snapshot.\n- [MEDIUM] — Preserve the stdio/0.15.0/temp-client boundary in all downstream synthesis; do not generalize to other transports or future persistent discovery.\n\nMeasured outcome passes the central question: K=0 remains 0/0 through N=50 and N=20/K=3 leaves exactly three called pairs resident before teardown. Conditional status is for evidence completeness, not a contradiction of the outcome.","created_at":"2026-08-08T23:36:28.202641189Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:5YGswZ1VqQhMX1kv2ooYreUQqAdLtPWo8YiQ+FMknzI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgLcAEc8XQBuylGyIaiBaeGtTKFiJUdqGspQDMBDK3R4MAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAy46O0etscv0NmC00GG7JCBbzDQERtqz+wbrGdyHSpizsov2/Y0sJ/SClgxi7sFEk1XJBzeORdirp0CINqPCgCA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:5YGswZ1VqQhMX1kv2ooYreUQqAdLtPWo8YiQ+FMknzI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgLcAEc8XQBuylGyIaiBaeGtTKFiJUdqGspQDMBDK3R4MAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLz2kDI9bVGm/kahm2tSunsmE4gSr8WT/PyPunwrZQ9oVK6M7Uj6YpIPzn2CBFRJvorze9wrnOegqdq3ikI1DAI="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-VAPd-validation-task-evidence-only-measurement-not-a-9948","agent_seq":17,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T23:36:41.305676088Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"5eb1d70d-2fa4-4cbd-9c71-9263c9e4dd6a","comment_uuid":"dc40703f-b8d7-4210-a26f-dd560d79b8fe","author":"pp3g-VAPd-validation-task-evidence-only-measurement-not-a-9948","content":"## Audit Verdict: PASS\n\n### 1. OUTCOME QUALITY — [OK] Evidence-backed validation with one minor data-quality gap\n\n**Test 1 — backend_spawn_count==0 re-verified:**\n- n1: backend_spawn_count=0, resident_after proxy_count=0/backend_count=0 (logs/test1/n1/test1-n1.json:14)\n- n5: backend_spawn_count=0, resident_after 0/0 (logs/test1/n5/test1-n5.json:14)\n- n10: backend_spawn_count=0, resident_after 0/0 (logs/test1/n10/test1-n10.json:14)\n- n20: backend_spawn_count=0, resident_after 0/0 (logs/test1/n20/test1-n20.json:14)\n- n50: backend_spawn_count=0, resident_after 0/0 (logs/test1/n50/test1-n50.json:14)\n- PASS criterion (backend_spawn_count==0) confirmed at every N. ✓\n\n**Test 2 — Peak vs resident-after properly separated:**\n- CondA (no teardown): peak_proxies=1, resident_after proxy_count=0/backend_count=0, backend_spawn_count=0 (logs/test2/test2-condA.json:19-29)\n- CondB (immediate teardown): peak_proxies=2, resident_after proxy_count=0/backend_count=0, backend_spawn_count=0 (logs/test2/test2-condB.json:19-29)\n- Report correctly notes peak=2 under load is transient and not decisive. ✓\n\n**Test 3 — 20-row sweep table re-verified (proxy/backend counts NOT collapsed):**\n- n1-sequential-off: peak_proxies=1, resident_after 0/0, backend_spawn_count=0 (logs/test3/n1-sequential-off.json)\n- n20-concurrent-on: peak_proxies=20, resident_after 0/0, backend_spawn_count=0 (logs/test3/n20-concurrent-on.json)\n- n50-sequential-off: peak_proxies=1, resident_after 0/0, backend_spawn_count=0 (logs/test3/n50-sequential-off.json)\n- Report table (report.md:216-237) records peak AND resident-after separately for proxies AND backends, with mode (sequential/concurrent) and teardown (off/on) per row. All 20 rows show resident-after = 0/0. ✓\n- Calling mode (sync/async) recorded per run. ✓\n\n**Test 4 — Three-category residency (the headline) re-verified:**\n- teardown-off: called_backends_resident=3, called_proxies_resident=3, refreshed_never_called_proxies_resident=0 (logs/test4/test4-teardown-off.json:87-102)\n- teardown-on: called_backends_resident=3, called_proxies_resident=3, refreshed_never_called_proxies_resident=0 (logs/test4/test4-teardown-on.json:105-120)\n- The 17-never-called headline row is PRESENT and SUPPORTED. ✓\n- Connector identity/reuse: c0 proxy PID 2572274 identical across call1/call2, backend PID 2572278 identical across call1/call2 (logs/test4/test4-teardown-off.json:36-42). Same pattern for c7 and c15. ✓\n- Explicit teardown reclaims everything: resident_after_teardown proxy_count=0/backend_count=0 (logs/test4/test4-teardown-on.json:87-93). ✓\n\n**Test 5a — list_changed gap characterized:**\n- Proxy emitted notification: sent notifications/tools/list_changed count=1 (logs/test5/5a/test5a.json:64, logs/test5/5a/a-proxy.log:21)\n- Registry catalog unchanged: catalog_changed=false (logs/test5/5a/test5a.json:11)\n- Backend tool set changed: control-5a.json shows only 'sub' tool (logs/test5/5a/control-5a.json)\n- No re-list from ToolRegistry after notification. ✓\n\n**Test 5b — stale-catalog baseline:**\n- First use returns application-level error: unknown tool 'add' (logs/test5/5b/test5b.json:7)\n- New tool absent from catalog: KeyError (logs/test5/5b/test5b.json:9)\n- No drift detection. ✓\n\n**Test 6 — immediate teardown boundary:**\n- Catalog-refresh N=10 K=0: resident 0/0 with and without teardown (logs/test6/test6.json:7-37)\n- After 1 call K=1: resident 1 proxy + 1 backend (logs/test6/test6.json:39-59)\n- After teardown: resident 0/0 (logs/test6/test6.json:61-76)\n- Call result correct (3.0). ✓\n\n**Addendum B — daemon-thread + calling mode + persistence config:**\n- threadcheck: async-only = 1 thread (MainThread), async_runtime_threads=0; after sync call = 4 threads, async_runtime_threads=1 (logs/threadcheck/threadcheck.json)\n- Every Test 3/4/5/6 JSON records calling_mode (sync/async), versions, grace_seconds. ✓\n- Persistence config: persistent=True default, verified against source (report.md:73-79). ✓\n\n**Pinned versions:**\n- toolregistry==0.15.0, mcp==2.0.0, python==3.10.12 recorded in Test 3/4/5/6 JSONs and threadcheck.json. ✓\n\n**CONCERN — versions field absent from Test 1 and Test 2 JSONs:**\n- Report claims 'Versions re-confirmed per run via importlib.metadata and recorded in every per-run JSON result (versions field)' (report.md:69-70).\n- Test 1 JSONs (n1, n5, n10, n20, n50) and Test 2 JSONs (condA, condB) do NOT contain a versions field.\n- Test 3/4/5/6/threadcheck JSONs DO contain versions.\n- Impact: LOW. The versions were consistent across all runs (verified by proxy log timestamps and the venv reuse note). The gap is a data-completeness issue, not a correctness issue. The common.py versions() function exists but was not called in the Test 1/2 scripts.\n\n**Orphan-process finding handled correctly:**\n- common.py clean_orphans() kills orphans BEFORE each test baseline (common.py:250-288).\n- Report documents the lifecycle finding (report.md:407-415): connectors orphan indefinitely in ep_poll on owner death without explicit close.\n- Orphans are NOT counted as resident — they are killed before measurement. ✓\n\n**Strong-pass criterion correctly applied:**\n- Report correctly uses 'bounded by workload/lifecycle policy, not proportional to N' (report.md:371-373, Addendum C).\n- NOT claiming literal resident-count==K identity. ✓\n\n### 2. PROCESS QUALITY — [OK] Workflow followed with minor gap\n\n- Commit 00eda4b3 references gh#295 in message. ✓\n- YAML front matter: program=EDASES, layer=Research, document_type=Research Finding, status=Validated, authority=Experimental (report.md:1-25). ✓\n- Observations vs findings separated throughout (explicit labels in each test section). ✓\n- Exact versions + calling mode + persistence config recorded per run. ✓\n- All 6 tests present with required data tables. ✓\n- One-sentence scaling conclusion (report.md:347-353). ✓\n- Architectural conclusion per Strong/Conditional/Fail (report.md:360-388). ✓\n- stdio-only scope respected (report.md:89-90, 139-147). ✓\n- Out-of-scope items explicitly listed (idle-timeout, non-stdio transports, invalidation design). ✓\n- 567 files committed (scripts, logs, report, proxy/backend implementations). ✓\n\n### 3. ARCHITECTURAL FIT — [OK] Respects identifier-first framing\n\n- Report stays at research-evidence layer: measures and reports, does not prescribe methodology or implementation.\n- The catalog/backend separation claim (knowing N without running N) is the core claim, correctly framed as experimental validation.\n- Temp-client discovery mechanism documented as the enabling property (report.md:95-107).\n- Caveats correctly prevent overclaiming: stdio only, ToolRegistry 0.15.0-specific, host-load caveat for timings.\n\n### 4. SYSTEMIC RISKS IDENTIFIED\n\n1. **Orphan-on-owner-death finding** — Impact: connector processes persist indefinitely if owning process exits without explicit close. The mcp 2.0.0 stdio server does not terminate on bare EOF. Recommended mitigation: document as a lifecycle constraint for the session-boundary runtime; track as a potential upstream mcp issue. Priority: MEDIUM (constrains runtime design but not blocking current validation).\n\n2. **list_changed gap** — Impact: ToolRegistry 0.15.0 does not consume notifications/tools/list_changed. This is a widely-documented gap across major MCP clients. Recommended mitigation: already characterized; track for epic #212 as a known limitation. Priority: LOW (characterized, not a bug to fix).\n\n3. **1-shared-thread sync model** — Impact: all sync API calls funnel through a single AsyncRuntime event loop, serializing concurrent sync calls. Recommended mitigation: document as a design constraint; concurrent workloads must use async API. Priority: LOW (observed and documented).\n\n4. **Versions field missing from Test 1/2 JSONs** — Impact: minor data-completeness gap. The versions() function in common.py exists but was not called in run_test1.py/run_test2.py. Recommended mitigation: add versions to all test scripts for consistency. Priority: LOW.\n\n### 5. RECOMMENDATIONS\n\n1. **Add versions field to Test 1 and Test 2 JSON outputs** — Rationale: report claims versions recorded in every per-run JSON; 7 of 27 JSON files lack it. A one-line common.versions() call in run_test1.py and run_test2.py would close the gap. Priority: LOW.\n\n2. **Consider adding a post-parent-death residency test** — Rationale: the orphan finding (report.md:407-415) is documented as an observation but was not a planned test. A dedicated test that verifies orphan behavior (spawn connectors, kill parent without close, measure persistence) would strengthen the lifecycle-finding evidence. Priority: LOW (finding is already well-documented with 3 independent observations).\n\n3. **Cross-reference orphan finding with epic #212** — Rationale: the orphan-on-owner-death constraint directly affects the session-boundary runtime design tracked in epic #212. Ensuring this finding is captured in the epic's known-issues list would prevent it from being lost. Priority: MEDIUM.","created_at":"2026-08-08T23:36:41.296856138Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:5YGswZ1VqQhMX1kv2ooYreUQqAdLtPWo8YiQ+FMknzI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgLcAEc8XQBuylGyIaiBaeGtTKFiJUdqGspQDMBDK3R4MAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA0Xy4j1USNp8eXpXIODctZtVNX8W/QrG0aPStpQE6nDQ6OeHDKq2KtE+yFfwqY4ppQMUOxLCKodR9W8qnuL2TCg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:5YGswZ1VqQhMX1kv2ooYreUQqAdLtPWo8YiQ+FMknzI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgLcAEc8XQBuylGyIaiBaeGtTKFiJUdqGspQDMBDK3R4MAAAAPY3Jvc3