{"agent_id":"pp3g-VAPd-validation-task-evidence-only-measurement-not-a-9948","agent_seq":38,"timestamp":"2026-08-09T01:31:05.015975080Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"44a2f894-85dc-4396-a3c6-66dbc327ec3b","comment_uuid":"b1a3a63e-d71e-41b0-b1b5-78021f505fd9","author":"pp3g-VAPd-validation-task-evidence-only-measurement-not-a-9948","content":"Captured from catalog-scale validation (#295 settle #306): three further connector-lifecycle constraints, version-bound to toolregistry 0.15.0 / mcp 2.0.0, now documented in the umbrella doc's Connector-lifecycle constraints section (docs/research/Identifier-First Tool Calling.md):\n\n1. ORPHAN-ON-OWNER-DEATH: connector proxy+backend processes persist indefinitely when the ToolRegistry process exits without explicit close (blocked in ep_poll, stdin at EOF; mcp 2.0.0 stdio server does not terminate on bare EOF). Deliberately reproduced and committed as logs/owner-death/owner-death-lifecycle.json (catalog-scale): 3 proxies + 3 backends survived owner SIGKILL through a 5s observation interval; reclamation required explicit TERM. Implication: lifecycle policy must own explicit teardown; process death alone is not sufficient reclamation.\n\n2. list_changed CONSUMPTION GAP: ToolRegistry 0.15.0 registers no message handler and has zero list_changed code (grep-verified; SDK parses the notification at mcp_types/methods.py:217). Backend-emitted tools/list_changed is invisible to the registry — catalog unchanged, no re-list, fresh refresh returns stale static manifest. This is the invalidation half of the output-schema-drift problem.\n\n3. 1-SHARED-THREAD SYNC MODEL: all sync-mode entry points serialize through ONE process-wide AsyncRuntime daemon thread (_async_runtime.py:65,72); count is exactly 1 at every N (1-50), never grows with N. Sync API cannot be truly concurrent; 'one thread per connector' must not be assumed.\n\nRe-validation trigger #279 (upgrade check) covers these alongside the C2-gap constraints.","created_at